const defaultRecipes = [{"id":1,"title":"Pistachio Chocolate Chickpea Cookies","description":"If you love cookies and want a change, try these. Soft, nutty, packed with pistachio and chocolate, you’d never guess they contain chickpeas. Minimal effort, maximum satisfaction.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"15 mins","servings":"3","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["1 can chickpeas, drained and rinsed","1 egg","40 g pistachio chocolate protein powder","30 g pistachio butter","½ teaspoon baking soda","1 tablespoon erythritol, or your preferred sweetener","15 g pistachio chocolate chunks","5 g ground pistachios"],"steps":["Heat oven to 180°C (160°C fan) and line a baking tray. Add all ingredients (except chocolate chunks and ground pistachios) to a blender or food processor.","Blend until smooth and thick, scraping down sides if needed. Spoon onto tray and shape into 8 cookies.","Press chocolate chunks onto each cookie, then sprinkle ground pistachios. Bake for 12–15 minutes until golden and set.","Let cookies cool completely on the tray so they firm up.","Sprinkle ground pistachios for crunch. Bake 12–15 minutes until golden and set.","Leave the cookies to cool completely on the tray for at least 20 minutes. They will firm up as they cool, so avoid moving them until they’re set and easy to lift.","That’s it. Enjoy!"],"tips":["Make these with lemon meringue chickpea cookies. Same blender, same oven, two flavours, minimal extra effort."],"cost":3.4},{"id":2,"title":"Lemon Meringue Chickpea Cookies","description":"These are soft, zesty cookies that taste like lemon meringue pie, but with almost no effort. Trust me, you’ll be amazed how good they are.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"15 mins","servings":"3","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["1 can chickpeas, drained and rinsed","1 egg","40 g lemon meringue protein powder","½ teaspoon baking soda","1 tablespoon erythritol, or your preferred sweetener","1 teaspoon lemon juice","15 g white chocolate lemon chunks","Zest of 1 lemon"],"steps":["Preheat oven to 180°C (160°C fan). Line a baking tray with baking paper.","Drain and rinse chickpeas thoroughly to remove tinned taste.","Add chickpeas, egg, protein powder, baking soda, sweetener, and lemon juice to blender or food processor.","Blend until smooth and thick, scraping the sides as needed.","Spoon mixture onto tray; shape into 8 cookies.","Press chocolate lemon chunks on top of each cookie.","Sprinkle lemon zest over cookies.","Bake 12–15 minutes, until cookies are golden and set.","Cool cookies on the tray, firming up.","Enjoy your cookies."],"tips":["Make the pistachio-chocolate version at the same time, and you get two flavours in one go. Same blender, same oven, barely any extra effort."],"cost":2.29},{"id":3,"title":"Watermelon Jelly Bowl","description":"This dessert looks like it took hours, but it only takes fruit and jelly in a watermelon shell. The sweet, colourful treat impresses guests with zero fuss.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"130 mins","servings":"8","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["Half a medium watermelon (about 1.5 kg)","2 sachets strawberry jelly (sugar-free or regular, up to you)","100 ml boiling water","A few drops of stevia or your favourite sweetener (optional)","100 g frozen strawberries","100 g raspberries","100 g blueberries"],"steps":["Slice the watermelon in half. Scoop out the flesh with a spoon.","Save the empty shell, your show-off bowl. It always gets a wow.","Set aside half the watermelon for snacking or another recipe-no waste.","Blend the remaining watermelon until smooth. Aim for about 600 ml of juice.","Boil the kettle. Pour 100 ml of the boiling water into a jug.","Tip the jelly sachets and stir until they dissolve completely.","Pour in the watermelon juice and mix thoroughly.","Add sweetener if you like. Taste and adjust as needed.","Throw the frozen berries directly into your watermelon bowl. Don’t defrost them.","Pour the jelly mixture over the fruit.","Place the watermelon bowl carefully in the fridge.","Chill for about 2 hours, or until the dessert sets.","Slice or scoop out generous portions. Let everyone enjoy plenty.","Dig in and enjoy your creation."],"tips":["Place the empty watermelon shell in a bowl before filling. This keeps things steady and saves you from a wobbly disaster."],"cost":6.5},{"id":4,"title":"Granola Clusters","description":"I first made this to clear out the random bits in my cupboard, and now I honestly make it every single week. Trust me, once you try it, you’ll get why.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"25 mins","servings":"10","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["100g jumbo oats (or regular porridge oats if that’s what you’ve got)","40g coconut flakes (or desiccated coconut works too)","70g chia seeds (if you don’t have any, just chuck in a bit more oats instead)","70g mixed seeds (pumpkin, sunflower, or honestly, whatever’s lurking in your cupboard)","60g cashew nuts (or swap for peanuts, walnuts, or whatever’s cheapest)","60g sunflower seeds","50g flaked almonds (or just throw in more mixed seeds if that’s easier)","1 tablespoon cashew butter (or peanut butter, or whatever nut butter you’ve got knocking about)","1 tablespoon pistachio butter (or just use more of the same nut butter, no need to be fancy)"],"steps":["Get your oven on at 160–175°C fan. Line a baking tray with baking paper.","Throw all the oats, coconut, seeds, and nuts into a big bowl.","Add in your nut butters.","Mix it all up so everything’s nicely coated.","Spread the lot out on your tray in a nice even layer.","Bake for 12–18 minutes. Give it a stir halfway through so it toasts evenly.","Take it out when your kitchen smells amazing and it looks golden.","Let it cool for a few minutes – don’t let it go cold yet.","Scatter your chocolate pieces over the warm granola so they melt slightly. Let it cool completely so it goes nice and crunchy.","Break it up and store in a jar or any airtight tub.","Try not to eat it all in one go. No promises."],"tips":["Don’t wander off. Seeds and coconut can burn in seconds right at the end.","Looks fancy, but honestly takes five minutes to throw together. No chef skills required.","Spoon it over yoghurt, fruit, or ice cream, or just grab a handful straight from the jar whenever you fancy. That’s how we do it."],"cost":4.99},{"id":5,"title":"Crispy Tortilla Fajita","description":"Fast, healthy and ADHD-friendly, zero wasted effort, and it tastes like it came from a restaurant. A full 15g of garlic for serious flavour, plus a crispy, cheesy crust straight from the pan.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"15 mins","servings":"2","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["100g ground beef,","90g tortilla wrap","30g shredded mozzarella","110g mixed bell peppers","90g onion","15g fresh garlic","20g leek","15g fajita seasoning mix"],"steps":["Sauté the ground beef with the onion, leek, garlic, peppers and fajita seasoning until cooked through and fragrant.","Lay out the tortilla, cut it in half, fill with the mixture and fold.","Place a sheet of baking paper in the pan, sprinkle the mozzarella on top, then set the filled tortilla directly onto the cheese.","Toast 2-3 minutes on each side until the cheese forms a golden, crunchy crust."],"tips":["Don't skimp on the garlic - the full 15g is what makes this taste restaurant-level.","Make sure the pan is hot before adding the tortilla so the cheese crisps properly."],"cost":2.5},{"id":6,"title":"Pistachio Protein Cheesecake","description":"Creamy, rich and loaded with protein, no biscuit base, no faff, just pure pistachio flavour done properly.  Time","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","video":"https://www.tiktok.com/@basicchefs/video/7668413096334986518?_r=1&_t=ZN-98TPeB99dfa","time":"75 mins + 4 hrs chilling","servings":"8","difficulty":"Medium","ingredients":["500g Prezydent Twarog Sernikowy 3% (or any quark/curd cheese)","2 large eggs","40g Chocolate Pistachio Protein powder","20g cornflour","60-80g erythritol, or any sweetener you like","A few drops of vanilla stevia (or extra vanilla bean paste)","1 tsp vanilla bean paste (or seeds from 1 vanilla pod)","2-3 tbsp pistachio butter, for the topping","2 tbsp white chocolate spread, for the topping","30-40g crushed pistachios, for the topping"],"steps":["Blend the white cheese, eggs, protein powder, cornflour, sweetener, vanilla drops and vanilla paste until smooth and creamy.","Pour the mix into a lined cake tin.","Sit the tin in a bigger tray and pour hot water around it - this stops the cheesecake from cracking.","Bake at 160C for 55-65 minutes. The edges should look set but the middle should still have a gentle wobble.","Turn off the oven, crack the door open, and leave the cheesecake inside for 20 minutes.","Let it cool, then chill in the fridge for at least 4 hours, overnight is best.","Melt the pistachio butter and white chocolate spread, swirl over the cheesecake, then finish with crushed pistachios."],"tips":["Don't wait until the centre is completely firm - remove it once the edges are set but the middle still wobbles, it finishes setting as it cools.","Chill overnight for the creamiest texture and cleanest slices."],"cost":9.5},{"id":7,"title":"Prosciutto & Mozzarella Pinsa","description":"The ultimate fridge-raid dinner. A yellow-sticker pinsa topped with whatever's left in the fridge, the cooked veg becomes your sauce, so there's no passata, no extra pots, no faff.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"20 mins","servings":"2","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["230g ready-made pinsa base","1 large onion, sliced","1 bell pepper, sliced","2 medium tomatoes, chopped","40g grated mature cheese","125g light mozzarella","40g prosciutto (4 slices)","Small handful fresh chives","Black pepper","Garlic granules (optional)"],"steps":["Fry the onion, pepper and tomatoes in a pan over medium heat until soft, juicy and starting to caramelise.","Put the pinsa base on a baking tray, spread the cooked veg over the top as your sauce, then sprinkle over the grated cheese.","Tear the mozzarella over the top and add the prosciutto.","Bake at 200°C (180°C fan) for 8-10 minutes until the cheese is melted and the edges are crispy.","Scatter over loads of fresh chopped chives, slice and serve."],"tips":["Ready-made pinsa is your shortcut to pizza night in under 20 minutes - no dough, no waiting, just top and bake.","At the normal pinsa price this meal would cost around £6 - the yellow-sticker version brings it down to about £4.40."],"cost":4.4},{"id":8,"title":"15-Minute Beef & Tomato Penne","description":"The pasta dish you'll make faster than your takeaway arrives, and it tastes way better. Lean beef, a ridiculous amount of garlic and loads of fresh tomatoes turn into the sauce, no jar, no faff, just real food in 15 minutes.","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","time":"20 mins","servings":"4","difficulty":"Easy","ingredients":["500g penne pasta","500g 5% beef mince","600g baby plum tomatoes","1 medium onion, sliced","30g garlic (about 6 cloves), chopped","50g lighter mature cheese, grated","Salt","Black pepper","Smoked paprika","Italian herbs","Chilli flakes (optional)","Fresh basil (optional)"],"steps":["Boil the penne in salted water according to the packet instructions. Before draining, save a mug of the pasta water.","Fry the sliced onion and garlic in a splash of oil over medium-high heat for 2-3 minutes until soft.","Add the beef mince, season with salt, pepper, smoked paprika and Italian herbs, and cook until browned.","Tip in the tomatoes and cook for 4-5 minutes, squashing a few with your spoon and leaving some whole - that's your sauce.","Add the drained pasta to the pan with a splash of pasta water and toss until coated.","Serve topped with grated cheese and fresh basil."],"tips":["Don't bother making a separate sauce - the tomatoes, beef juices and a splash of pasta water do the job.","Don't be shy with the garlic - it makes the dish.","One pan, less washing up."],"cost":5.37}];

const defaultAbout = {"heading":"Who is Basic Chefs?","text":"We are Basic Chefs and we started our journey at home. Life was hard, and the kitchen was our safe place, it was our escape.\n\nThose simple home meals made us the cooks we are today. We learned that good food doesn't need fancy ingredients or high skillsets  just love and practice.\n\nBasic Chefs is for everyone. No complicated steps, no fancy talk just real food, made simple and most importantly, with outstanding taste, shared with you."};
